    "narrative": "For tonight\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** (73.47) and **Daulton Varsho** (68.37) stand as our premier assets. **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a massive 16% SP skill bump against Ure\u00f1a, while the park factors elevate **Daulton Varsho** into an elite tier despite a moderate matchup against Rea. **Bryson Stott** (63.77) also warrants attention; while he faces the tough Peralta, the slow delivery time of the opposing battery provides a rare, actionable boost to his stolen base probability\u2014a critical edge given our focus on scarcity in that category. These three represent our highest efficiency ceiling for the evening.\n\nIn terms of bench management, **Drew Gilbert** (39.49) was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine. While his platoon matchup against Meyer is favorable, his projected position at the bottom of the order creates a significant drag on his run-production potential, ultimately pushing him just below our 40-point \"Zebras Floor.\" We are also monitoring **Taylor Ward** (46.10) closely; while he earns a spot due to his leadoff status and favorable wind conditions, the matchup against Yamamoto is daunting. His score reflects a sharp decline due to the high skill level of the opposing starter, and we will be watching his early at-bats to see if the wind offsets the pitching disadvantage. \n\nFinally, remain mindful of the risk profile surrounding our catchers, **Cal Raleigh** (55.51) and **Yainer Diaz** (56.33). Both face high-caliber arms in Connelly and Cantillo, respectively, forcing us to rely on dynamic platoon edges to keep their projections in the \"Strong\" territory. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Will Smith**, and **Tyler Freeman** currently unavailable, our depth is being tested; we continue to monitor the utility bench for any late-breaking lineup shifts that might allow us to swap in reserves like **Ryan Waldschmidt**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Masyn Winn**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, or **Gavin Sheets** if their matchups improve unexpectedly.",
